    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DtCMR6qcoYVuswMQFkPCKF)_\n\nFollow-up to #173 for `rel-anno-fa2`.\n\n- **Room between nodes:** graph-fa2 lays nodes out without knowing label sizes, so labels overlapped. Nodes are now drawn `relationship-annotator-fa2-spread` (4) times farther apart on a canvas that many times larger (advice on `graph-fa2-normalise-coords` and its inverse, so drag and click still match). Labels keep their size, so zoom in to read. The engine is now `2d`: in 3d, nodes behind each other overlap whatever the spacing.\n- **Box behind each label:** a rounded box in the node's colour at 75% opacity (`relationship-annotator-fa2-box-opacity`); the text takes the theme foreground or background, whichever contrasts. graph-fa2 has no box option, so this post-processes its SVG (advice on `graph-fa2--render-svg`). I chose the box over making the box the node, because the circle still gives the layout and click target.\n- **Theme colours:** the node fill is the foreground of a theme face per tag group colour (`relationship-annotator-fa2-group-faces`: orange is `warning`, green is `success`, gray is `shadow`, ...), and text, edge labels and edges follow `default` and `shadow`. It reads the theme each time the command runs.\n\nTested in headless Emacs 29 with the real graph-fa2: the SVG gets the boxes, and across 12 to 60 boxes (2d), overlapping pairs went from 6 to 33 at spread 1 to none at spread 4. In 3d some still overlapped, hence the 2d engine. Not seen on screen: how the colours look on your themes and the zoom level. Literate doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9MFEtBRvJfg7M7vTd)_",
